      *> DESIGN EXAMPLE - NOT COMPILED OR PRODUCTION READY.
      *> Project-operation pseudocode; missing backend/SDK is intentional.
      *> Mapping: I004 Publisher; CAP-012..CAP-017.
      *> Tests: AT-013, AT-015..AT-019.
      *> CLAIM/ACK are short atomic backend operations.
      *> Network I/O must run outside business-record locks.

       PUBLISH-ONE-EVENT.
           PERFORM CLAIM-READY-EVENT-WITH-FENCING
           EVALUATE TRUE
               WHEN NO-ELIGIBLE-EVENT
                   PERFORM WAIT-WITHOUT-ADVANCING-PREFIX
               WHEN CLAIM-VALID
                   PERFORM SEND-FROZEN-ENVELOPE
                   EVALUATE TRUE
                       WHEN BROKER-DURABLE-ACCEPT
                           PERFORM ACK-WITH-CURRENT-LEASE-AND-FENCE
                           IF NOT ACK-DURABLE
                               PERFORM KEEP-FOR-RECOVERY
                           END-IF
                       WHEN SEND-AMBIGUOUS
                           PERFORM KEEP-FOR-RECOVERY
                       WHEN OTHER
                           PERFORM RECORD-ERROR-AND-SCHEDULE-RETRY
                   END-EVALUATE
               WHEN OTHER
                   PERFORM STOP-AND-REPORT
           END-EVALUATE.

      *> SEND uses the exact eventId, bytes and version stored in spool.
      *> A reconnect/retry must not create a new business event identity.
      *> Broker acceptance does not mean Cosmos application.
      *> ACK validates lease expiry/fence inside the same backend commit
      *> that records acknowledgement and advances only resolved prefix.
      *> Old worker ACK after a new claim -> STALE_FENCE; no state mutation.
      *> ACK 101 and 103, with 102 pending -> contiguous prefix remains 101.
      *> These numbers are local ledger examples, not IBM log positions.
      *> Lost ACK after successful SEND can duplicate delivery by design.
      *> Do not purge acknowledged spool before approved retention/replay.
